# Repo-root .dockerignore — governs the build context for
# nginx/Dockerfile (docker-compose.yml's `nginx` service uses
# `context: .`, the only image built from the repo root rather than
# server/, which has its own scoped .dockerignore).
#
# Without this file, the entire repo tree — every node_modules,
# .git history, any local .env files — was sent to the Docker daemon
# and available inside the build stage. Concretely dangerous here:
# nginx/Dockerfile's client build stage runs `npm ci` (installing a
# clean, Linux-correct node_modules) and then `COPY client/ .` — with
# no dockerignore, a host-machine client/node_modules (built for
# macOS/Windows, with platform-specific optional deps like Rollup's
# native binaries) would land in that COPY and silently overwrite the
# just-installed one, and a host client/.env (if one exists locally)
# would be copied in and baked into the built JS bundle right
# alongside it. See DECISIONS.md, "Task 39: two deployment topologies"
# for the broader Docker context this file supports.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.vite

.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.log
npm-debug.log*

.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea

coverage
*.rdb
dump.rdb

.claude
